{
  "case_id": "2016-15-1194",
  "document_hash": "4f8df18b7f97683a71a4a37b1a93545e58eb5ab57ced2c6b4b28d2917a2fa083",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1194",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f8df18b7f97683a71a4a37b1a93545e58eb5ab57ced2c6b4b28d2917a2fa083",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f8df18b7f97-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nDAVID T. GOLDBERG, ESQ., Stanford, Cal.; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nROBERT C. MONTGOMERY, ESQ., Senior Deputy Attorney General, Raleigh, N.C.; on behalf of the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1194",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f8df18b7f97683a71a4a37b1a93545e58eb5ab57ced2c6b4b28d2917a2fa083",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f8df18b7f97-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are three principal features of North Carolina's law that make it a stark abridgement of the Freedom of Speech.\nFirst, Section 202.5 reaches vast swaths of core First Amendment activity that is totally unrelated to the government's preventative purpose.\nMr. Packingham is not accused of communicating with or viewing the profile of a minor. He violated Section 202.5 by speaking to his friends and family about his experience in traffic court. And if today he were to view or respond to any of the thousands of Twitter messages about his case in this Court, that would be a felony."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1194",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f8df18b7f97683a71a4a37b1a93545e58eb5ab57ced2c6b4b28d2917a2fa083",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f8df18b7f97-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Could a State impose this restriction as a condition of parole?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1194",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f8df18b7f97683a71a4a37b1a93545e58eb5ab57ced2c6b4b28d2917a2fa083",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f8df18b7f97-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: What do you think your best argument is? Is this statute too overbroad? Does it fail scrutiny, whatever level we adopt? What's the --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1194",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f8df18b7f97683a71a4a37b1a93545e58eb5ab57ced2c6b4b28d2917a2fa083",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f8df18b7f97-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: -- doctrinal choices you offer us to say why this is unconstitutional?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1194",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f8df18b7f97683a71a4a37b1a93545e58eb5ab57ced2c6b4b28d2917a2fa083",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f8df18b7f97-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Well, one of the -- I mean, under narrow tailoring, I think it's -- it's incumbent upon you to come up with a narrow -- more narrowly tailored alternative."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1194",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f8df18b7f97683a71a4a37b1a93545e58eb5ab57ced2c6b4b28d2917a2fa083",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f8df18b7f97-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Go back to Justice Kennedy's question, if you would, which is, is there a capacity to determine the age of a user; meaning, is there a way for the State to be able to track whether or not a potential defendant is actually in communication with a minor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1194",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f8df18b7f97683a71a4a37b1a93545e58eb5ab57ced2c6b4b28d2917a2fa083",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f8df18b7f97-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Social networking, it includes Facebook, obviously; it includes LinkedIn; it includes Twitter; is that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Montgomery",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1194",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f8df18b7f97683a71a4a37b1a93545e58eb5ab57ced2c6b4b28d2917a2fa083",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f8df18b7f97-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MONTGOMERY: That -- that's correct, Justice Ginsburg. There is a prohibition on Facebook and on some of the other major commercial sites --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Montgomery",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1194",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f8df18b7f97683a71a4a37b1a93545e58eb5ab57ced2c6b4b28d2917a2fa083",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f8df18b7f97-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MONTGOMERY: The -- the legislature in North Carolina wanted to have some narrow tailoring to this -- to this statute. So the fact that it eliminates or exempts some of those things is really a virtue, not a vice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1194",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f8df18b7f97683a71a4a37b1a93545e58eb5ab57ced2c6b4b28d2917a2fa083",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f8df18b7f97-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Well, I would have -- I would have thought that Snapchat is -- is -- maybe I have it wrong. I'm not any expert on this. But isn't Snapchat photo sharing?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Montgomery",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1194",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f8df18b7f97683a71a4a37b1a93545e58eb5ab57ced2c6b4b28d2917a2fa083",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f8df18b7f97-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This case is much more like Burson v. Freeman, in which this Court said that this 100-foot buffer zone, that a campaign-free zone at a voting place was permissible. And that was suppressing political speech."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1194",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f8df18b7f97683a71a4a37b1a93545e58eb5ab57ced2c6b4b28d2917a2fa083",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f8df18b7f97-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is -- is a provision like this ever added to the sentences as opposed to following from the sex registry?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Montgomery",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1194",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f8df18b7f97683a71a4a37b1a93545e58eb5ab57ced2c6b4b28d2917a2fa083",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f8df18b7f97-0002-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Here is a situation in which you have sex offenders who have committed heinous crimes and are likely to recidivate."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1194",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f8df18b7f97683a71a4a37b1a93545e58eb5ab57ced2c6b4b28d2917a2fa083",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f8df18b7f97-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why? I got a page here with -- printed from nytimes.com, from the New York Times, where on the side there's commentary by people who have created profiles on themselves having a public discussion between them on a news article that was printed in the New York Times."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1194",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4f8df18b7f97683a71a4a37b1a93545e58eb5ab57ced2c6b4b28d2917a2fa083",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4f8df18b7f97-0002-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2016-15-1194",
